body:
Part of #290 (design decisions D1-D10 in its research comment).

Depends on: #531.

The first wire op (D1). A vertical cut along a contour:
- offset by the wire radius plus the condition's gap;
- explicit **punch / die** side parameter, never inferred (folded in per D8);
- lead-in/out from a stated **start hole / threading point**;
- **corner strategy:** minimum internal radius is wire radius + gap, and a smaller corner is refused by name (folded in per D8).

Moves carry no pose, so the cut posts as XY (D2). Refusals: an enclosed profile without a start hole; a missing wire diameter, gap or condition (at command creation).

**Done means:** a die and a punch on the same profile offset to opposite sides by exactly the kerf. A too-tight corner and a missing start hole are refused by name. CL golden committed.
